  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increased labour market relevance of skills development</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ILO will support the Ministry of Education and Science of Ukraine and the Ministry of Economy, Agriculture and Environment of Ukraine in strengthening the labour-market relevance of skills development by expanding access to modern, flexible and demand-driven training for young people and adults. With extensive damage to educational infrastructure and growing shortages of skilled labour, particularly in occupations critical for reconstruction, recovery and the green transition, the digitalisation of training has become essential to ensure continuity of learning and to provide safe training opportunities in areas affected by hostilities. Building on previous achievements, including the digitalisation of TVET curricula, the development of e-pedagogy for teachers and the expansion of the profosvita.online platform, the intervention will support the scale-up of high-quality online, blended and work-based training programmes. This will include the development of labour-market-responsive curricula for re-skilling and up-skilling, support to TVET institutions to modernise their training offer and infrastructure, and strengthened teacher competencies in digital and innovative pedagogies.
The ILO will also promote inclusive and gender-responsive skills development to ensure that women and vulnerable groups can acquire skills for non-traditional and high-demand occupations. Innovative modalities, such as virtual and augmented reality training and micro-credentials, will be expanded to facilitate rapid acquisition of skills aligned with emerging technologies and reconstruction needs. Together, these measures will contribute to a more resilient, future-oriented and labour-market-responsive lifelong learning system capable of meeting Ukraine&#x2019;s evolving skills demands.</narrative>
  </description>
